	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  authentification]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=33989#p33989"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>merci pour votre retour, voilà le contenu de mon pg_hba.conf. Pour le mot de passe j&#039;ai utilisé celui que j&#039;ai crée lors de l&#039;installation de Postgres et je ne sais pas s&#039;il est correct ou si je devrait utiliser un autre à la place</p><br /><br /><p># TYPE&#160; DATABASE&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; USER&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ADDRESS&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;METHOD</p><p># &quot;local&quot; is for Unix domain socket connections only<br />local&#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256<br /># IPv4 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; scram-sha-256<br /># IPv6 local connections:<br />host&#160; &#160; all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256<br /># Allow replication connections from localhost, by a user with the<br /># replication privilege.<br />local&#160; &#160;replication&#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256<br />host&#160; &#160; replication&#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;127.0.0.1/32&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; scram-sha-256<br />host&#160; &#160; replication&#160; &#160; &#160;all&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;::1/128&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;scram-sha-256</p>]]></content>
